Given the many [[Phenomena/Althane/Cycle|cycles]] that passed before this one, there should be vast amounts of ancient knowledge spread throughout the world. Despite this, only a smattering of writing appears to have made the transition from previous cycles to this one. The Trust is a collection of scholars who aim to discover what causes the loss of information, why some things aren't affected, and how they can preserve their knowledge of past cycles in the future. To this end, they collect as much of the writing from past cycles as they can, and store them in the great arcanums they have across the continent.

Its head was long [[People/Althane/The Crystalpoint Lattice|the Crystalpoint Lattice]], the sentient artifact that ruled [[Geography/Althane/Illyara/index|Illyara]], and the Trust had no way to choose a successor; when the Lattice was excised and left floating in space, the organization was left without a ruler for the first time. [[People/Althane/Divex|Divex]] set [[People/Althane/Oxus|Oxus]] over it, and the Trust is now one of the seats of learning gathered into [[Org/Althane/X-Dive|X-Dive]].

### The Arcanum

The Trust maintains an Arcanum in most large cities they have a major presence in. Members of the Trust have complete access to the Arcanums at their leisure, while non-members may be granted access to some parts, under the watchful eye of a guild member.
